00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:54.693
- Jenn Shifferd wants to know this.

00:03:55.688 --> 00:03:57.620
"Don't we already use
satellites for military action?

00:03:57.620 --> 00:04:01.800
What other ways will
they militarize space?"

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:04.050
- Yeah when people think of
the militarization of space

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:06.945
they're often thinking of
Star Wars, weapons, missiles

00:04:06.945 --> 00:04:08.310
and things.

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:10.790
Problem is when you're
in space and in orbit

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:14.450
you're going 18,000 miles
an hour in low earth orbit.

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:16.240
If you start busting stuff up,

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:19.355
now you have particles and bits and pieces

00:04:19.355 --> 00:04:21.820
of formerly operating satellites,

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:24.780
that are themselves projectiles,

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:27.220
moving at 18,000 miles per hour.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:30.560
And so, you make a mess of things.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:33.340
So space war would last
a few hours and then

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:35.490
you'd never have another space war again.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:36.430
(laughing)

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:40.516
So, space has been the
repository of spy satellites

00:04:40.516 --> 00:04:42.440
ever since we've had satellites.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:44.820
And in that sense, it
has been militarized.

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:48.700
If fact, the Gulf War of
2003 was completely enabled

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:53.700
by space assets, with GPS
satellites leading the way.

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:55.440
Which we think of as just helping you get

00:04:55.440 --> 00:05:00.060
to grandma's house in your
car, but it was conceived,

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:02.390
launched and operated by the military,

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:06.430
and was later co-opted
by business interests.

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:10.770
So it'll find grandma's house, Uber,

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:12.940
their entire business model depends on it,

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:16.610
and if you wanna find
a mate within 1.5 miles

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:19.410
of your location, swipe right.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:20.950
- Interplanetary hook ups.

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:22.691
I like the way you think, Neil.

